Subject: [PATCH] drm/msm: retain O82 VRR when fixed modes fall below its floor

Aggregate connector VRR metadata from modes admitted by the existing encoder
callback. A fixed mode below the requested floor must not suppress the range
of other eligible modes. Atomic validation still rejects VRR for an ineligible
mode; foreign hardware, an empty eligible set, inconsistent positive floors
and a range without variation retain their refusal paths.

This enables a bounded higher-floor touch experiment. It does not establish
optical panel cadence or physical touch acceptance.

Expose a read-only floor-policy API version so userspace can distinguish this
mode-dependent range implementation from earlier all-modes-only metadata.

--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/dsi/dsi_manager.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/dsi/dsi_manager.c
@@ -1197,7 +1197,9 @@
 		list_for_each_entry(mode, &connector->probed_modes, head) {
 			floor = priv->kms->funcs->get_vrr_min_hz(encoder, mode);
-			if (!floor || (min_hz && min_hz != floor))
+			if (!floor)
+				continue;
+			if (min_hz && min_hz != floor)
 				return;
 			min_hz = floor;
 			max_hz = max_t(unsigned int, max_hz, drm_mode_vrefresh(mode));
 		}
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/disp/dpu1/dpu_encoder.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/disp/dpu1/dpu_encoder.c
@@ -227,2 +227,5 @@
 static unsigned int o82_vrr_test_min_hz;
 module_param(o82_vrr_test_min_hz, uint, 0400);
+static unsigned int o82_vrr_floor_api = 1;
+module_param(o82_vrr_floor_api, uint, 0400);
+MODULE_PARM_DESC(o82_vrr_floor_api, "O82 eligible-mode VRR floor policy API version");
